1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,170
Most investors don't lose money

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:03,980
because they picked the wrong fund.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,350
They lose it through a few classic mistakes.

4
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:08,810
There are twelve of them.

5
00:00:08,830 --> 00:00:11,270
And almost every investor makes at least one.

6
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:14,030
Each one is easy to make.

7
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:14,770
And each one

8
00:00:14,790 --> 00:00:16,670
can cost you thousands of euros.

9
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:20,320
Morningstar found that fund investors earned

10
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:22,700
about 1.2 percentage points a year

11
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,040
less than their own funds,

12
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:26,320
just because of when they bought and sold.

13
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,530
No hype, and no stock picks.

14
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:32,110
This is education, not financial advice.

15
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,070
Let's open the first box.

16
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:37,170
Mistake 1.

17
00:00:37,190 --> 00:00:38,360
Waiting to start.

18
00:00:39,670 --> 00:00:40,520
It feels safer

19
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:41,900
to wait for the right moment,

20
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,300
or a better salary.

21
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,520
But waiting is often

22
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:46,510
the most expensive mistake of all.

23
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,750
With €200 a month at 7% a year,

24
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:56,140
starting at 25 gives about €244,000 at 55.

25
00:00:56,160 --> 00:01:00,120
Starting at 35 gives about €104,000.

26
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:03,040
Ten years of waiting cost more

27
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:04,630
than half of the final amount.

28
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:07,810
The first euros you invest have

29
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:08,940
the most time to grow.

30
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,990
And you don't need a lot to start.

31
00:01:11,010 --> 00:01:13,530
Many brokers accept a few euros a month.

32
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:15,610
Mistake 2.

33
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:16,840
No safety cushion.

34
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:20,320
Investing without an emergency fund

35
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:22,600
is like driving without a spare tyre.

36
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:24,700
The first flat forces you to stop.

37
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,900
Lose your job during a crash,

38
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:28,550
and you may have

39
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:30,630
to sell at the worst possible moment.

40
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:33,390
A common rule of thumb:

41
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:34,420
three to six months

42
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,350
of expenses in a savings account,

43
00:01:36,370 --> 00:01:37,420
before you invest.

44
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:40,730
A cushion doesn't just protect your money.

45
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:42,200
It protects your nerves.

46
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:44,400
Mistake 3.

47
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:46,080
Investing money you need soon.

48
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:49,400
Money for a house deposit next year,

49
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:50,180
or a wedding,

50
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:52,160
doesn't belong in the stock market.

51
00:01:53,470 --> 00:01:54,360
Markets can drop

52
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:55,760
by a third in a few weeks,

53
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:57,140
like in 2020.

54
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,120
And they don't care about your deadline.

55
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:01,400
A simple rule:

56
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:02,690
money you need within a few

57
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:04,660
years stays out of the stock market.

58
00:02:05,970 --> 00:02:06,850
For short goals,

59
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:09,270
a savings account or a money market fund

60
00:02:09,290 --> 00:02:10,920
is usually the calmer place.

61
00:02:12,230 --> 00:02:13,070
Mistake 4.

62
00:02:13,090 --> 00:02:14,210
Paying high fees.

63
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:18,520
A fee of 1.8% a year sounds small.

64
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:20,410
Over thirty years, it isn't.

65
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:24,420
On €200 a month for 30 years,

66
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:27,910
the gap between a 0.03% ETF

67
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:30,090
and a 1.8% fund

68
00:02:30,110 --> 00:02:32,480
can be more than €60,000.

69
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:35,480
Fees hide in many places.

70
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,860
The fund's yearly fee,

71
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:39,340
entry fees, broker fees, currency fees.

72
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:42,030
Every euro paid in fees

73
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:44,470
is a euro that stops compounding for you.

74
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:47,400
You can't control the market.

75
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:49,040
You can control what you pay.

76
00:02:50,330 --> 00:02:51,190
Mistake 5.

77
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,430
Timing the market.

78
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:55,110
Sell before the crash,

79
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:56,460
buy back before the recovery.

80
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:57,750
It sounds easy.

81
00:02:57,770 --> 00:02:59,840
Almost nobody gets both right.

82
00:03:01,130 --> 00:03:02,370
In one J.P.

83
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:03,570
Morgan study of the S&P

84
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:07,470
500 from 1995 to 2014,

85
00:03:07,490 --> 00:03:11,260
staying invested earned about 9.9% a year.

86
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,290
Missing just the ten best days cut

87
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:15,200
that to 6.1%.

88
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,540
And many of the best days came right

89
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,670
after the worst ones.

90
00:03:19,690 --> 00:03:21,620
To catch them, you have to stay in.

91
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:25,050
Even professionals rarely manage it.

92
00:03:25,070 --> 00:03:26,750
Over the long run,

93
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:28,450
most active funds lag their index.

94
00:03:29,770 --> 00:03:30,560
Mistake 6.

95
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:31,530
Panic selling.

96
00:03:32,830 --> 00:03:34,280
In early 2020,

97
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,160
the S&P 500 fell

98
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:38,050
by about a third in a few weeks.

99
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:39,720
Millions of people sold.

100
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,960
About five months after the bottom,

101
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,530
it was back at its old high.

102
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:46,480
Those who sold missed the rebound.

103
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,180
Selling turns a temporary

104
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:50,660
drop into a permanent loss.

105
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:54,190
Writing your plan down before a crash makes

106
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:56,040
it much easier to follow during one.

107
00:03:57,330 --> 00:03:58,330
Mistake 7.

108
00:03:58,350 --> 00:03:59,910
Chasing last year's winners.

109
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,530
Last year's best fund

110
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:03,810
looks like a sure thing.

111
00:04:03,830 --> 00:04:05,060
It usually isn't.

112
00:04:06,370 --> 00:04:07,610
Of the US stock funds

113
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:09,830
in the top quarter in 2019,

114
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:12,630
only 2.2% stayed in the top quarter

115
00:04:12,650 --> 00:04:14,310
in each of the next two years.

116
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,680
By the time a fund

117
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,500
or a theme is in the headlines,

118
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:19,580
a lot of the gains

119
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:20,750
are often behind it.

120
00:04:22,070 --> 00:04:24,130
Investors pile in after the gains,

121
00:04:24,150 --> 00:04:26,080
and pile out after the losses.

122
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:29,370
That's exactly how the 1.2 point gap happens.

123
00:04:30,670 --> 00:04:31,440
Mistake 8.

124
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:33,160
Putting everything on one bet.

125
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:36,780
From 1926 to 2016,

126
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:39,310
just 4% of US stocks created all

127
00:04:39,330 --> 00:04:41,350
the net wealth of the stock market.

128
00:04:41,370 --> 00:04:42,320
More than half did

129
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:44,520
worse than short-term government bills.

130
00:04:45,830 --> 00:04:47,020
In 2020, Wirecard,

131
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:49,490
a company in Germany's top index,

132
00:04:49,510 --> 00:04:52,610
collapsed after €1.9 billion turned out

133
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:53,510
to be missing.

134
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:56,030
Owning one company,

135
00:04:56,050 --> 00:04:57,800
even a famous one, is a bet.

136
00:04:57,820 --> 00:04:59,600
Owning thousands is a plan.

137
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:02,990
That includes the company you work for.

138
00:05:03,010 --> 00:05:04,140
If it fails,

139
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:04,980
you can lose your job

140
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,910
and your savings at the same time.

141
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,020
Mistake 9.

142
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,140
Trading too much.

143
00:05:11,430 --> 00:05:13,050
A famous study of more than

144
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:16,030
66,000 households found that those who

145
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:19,110
traded the most earned 11.4% a year.

146
00:05:19,130 --> 00:05:22,070
The market earned 17.9%.

147
00:05:23,370 --> 00:05:26,950
Every trade costs fees, spreads, sometimes taxes.

148
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:28,500
And checking your account every day

149
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:29,890
makes you want to act.

150
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,340
Often, the best thing to do is nothing.

151
00:05:34,630 --> 00:05:36,660
In that study, the more people traded,

152
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,650
the less they earned.

153
00:05:38,930 --> 00:05:39,650
Mistake 10.

154
00:05:39,670 --> 00:05:40,840
Following the hype.

155
00:05:42,130 --> 00:05:43,660
A tip from social media,

156
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:45,710
the stock everyone is talking about,

157
00:05:45,730 --> 00:05:47,530
a friend who got rich last month.

158
00:05:48,830 --> 00:05:50,470
In January 2021,

159
00:05:50,490 --> 00:05:52,320
GameStop shares rose more than

160
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:53,840
tenfold in a few weeks.

161
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:54,730
Within a month,

162
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:56,310
most of those gains were gone.

163
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,290
If you hear about it from everyone,

164
00:05:59,310 --> 00:06:00,630
you're probably not early.

165
00:06:01,930 --> 00:06:03,970
Hype is also where scams hide.

166
00:06:03,990 --> 00:06:06,900
Guaranteed returns, urgency, a famous face.

167
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,320
Mistake 11.

168
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:11,050
Buying what you don't understand.

169
00:06:12,330 --> 00:06:13,790
Leveraged ETFs, CFDs,

170
00:06:13,810 --> 00:06:17,290
structured products with a fancy coupon.

171
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:19,580
If you can't explain how it makes money,

172
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:20,700
that's a warning sign.

173
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,690
Complex products are often built

174
00:06:23,710 --> 00:06:25,520
to make money for the seller first.

175
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:27,780
A simple test:

176
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,960
could you explain it

177
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,410
to a friend in two sentences?

178
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:31,500
If not, wait.

179
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:33,650
Mistake 12.

180
00:06:33,670 --> 00:06:35,060
Using the wrong account.

181
00:06:36,370 --> 00:06:38,010
Investing in a regular account

182
00:06:38,030 --> 00:06:40,150
when your country offers a tax-free one

183
00:06:40,170 --> 00:06:41,940
can cost you thousands over time.

184
00:06:43,230 --> 00:06:45,340
Same ETF, same market.

185
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,150
Different account, different result.

186
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:50,920
But watch out for products sold as tax-free

187
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:52,170
that come with high fees.

188
00:06:52,190 --> 00:06:54,700
The tax break can disappear in the costs.

189
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,980
We explain every type of investment

190
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,940
account in Europe in another video.

191
00:07:01,230 --> 00:07:02,940
Those are the twelve mistakes.

192
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:04,100
The good news:

193
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:04,530
most of them

194
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:06,470
are fixed by doing less, not more.

195
00:07:07,770 --> 00:07:08,500
Start early.

196
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:09,290
Keep a cushion.

197
00:07:09,310 --> 00:07:10,250
Pay low fees.

198
00:07:10,270 --> 00:07:11,400
And stay invested.

199
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,560
Markets can go down for years,

200
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:16,580
and nothing here is a recommendation.

201
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,710
This is not financial advice.

202
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,990
Which mistake have you already made?

203
00:07:22,010 --> 00:07:23,740
Most of us have made at least one.

204
00:07:25,030 --> 00:07:26,650
If this helped, subscribe.

205
00:07:26,670 --> 00:07:29,930
Next up, every investment account in Europe, explained.

